Use no more than 90% of stated capacity for planned work. The remaining 10% is slack.

## Weekly outcome

Preserve the learner's baseline, register candidate authoritative sources, and turn one diagnosed gap into a prerequisite-linked next action.

## Capacity allocation

| Order | Work | Share of weekly capacity | Evidence |
|---:|---|---:|---|
| 1 | Unaided first model and diagnostic sample | 25% | Untouched attempt plus actual time |
| 2 | Verify course scope and source candidates | 20% | Source register entries with rationale |
| 3 | Investigate the first diagnosed prerequisite | 25% | Notes plus one retrieval attempt |
| 4 | Re-attempt one diagnostic element | 10% | Before/after evidence |
| 5 | Weekly review and tracker update | 10% | Completed review linked to evidence |
| — | Unallocated slack | 10% | Not pre-spent |

## Ordered checklist

- [ ] Complete [TODAY.md](../TODAY.md) in order.
- [ ] Finish or deliberately stop the baseline diagnostic; record what remains unanswered.
- [ ] Verify at least one source and record its authority and version where applicable.
- [ ] Choose the highest-impact prerequisite exposed by the diagnostic.
- [ ] Practice that prerequisite within the capacity allocation.
- [ ] Re-attempt one baseline element without notes after a delay.
- [ ] Log actual time and evidence.
- [ ] Complete the weekly review before planning another week.

## Stop rule

Stop when the capacity ceiling is reached. Move unfinished work only after the review determines it still serves the active gate.
